 ## Background
-The NeRF training loop was introduced in "Neural Radiance Fields" by Mildenhall et al. (2020) [S1, S3, unofficial]. It builds on earlier work on coordinate-based neural representations [S2, unofficial]. The method has become a standard baseline for view synthesis and 3D reconstruction [S3, unofficial].
+The training procedure involves iterative optimization of a neural radiance field by sampling random rays per iteration, rendering predicted colors via volume integration, computing MSE loss against ground truth, and updating network weights via gradient descent [S4, unofficial]. It builds on coordinate-based neural representations [S2, unofficial].
 
